ng that there's clearly a problem in  society the question is what is he gonna  do about it for now all we get is aha  which is consistent with yellow guy's  reactions in previous episodes he's  naive uncertain absorbing ideas along  the way i suspect it has to do with the  brief shot of yellow guy with the banjo  it's important to note that up to this  point yellow guy has never been the one  singing the actual songs in the show  he's always getting bombarded with  everyone else's lessons but in this case  he's the one holding the instrument so  maybe we're at a point where we get to  hear what yellow guy finally has to say  he's stepping up and taking action maybe  this new series is the story of him  standing up and doing something for a  change he sees the fly and he has  something to say about it and then  there's duck like i mentioned before  duck's role in the series has always  been a bit unclear but it seems like the  creators recently have been interested  in exploring the character more  considering that both the deleted wakey  wakey trailer as well as in fly duck is  the one taken center stage though the  episode wakey wakey never aired  summaries of it appeared online after it  premiered at the sundance film festival  in it duck takes advantage of his  history as a well-known television  personality to step up and fill the  power vacuum left by the mayor's  disappearance he's manipulated by a  singing key into locking down the city  installing duck-billed cameras  everywhere to create a secure  surveillance state and he ultimately  blames everything bad that happens on  mysterious strangers who are coming to  get us he creates chaos by causing  people to suspect their neighbors and  when anyone descends duck drills into  the heads of the locals in order to  brainwash them into repeating everything  he says at the time wakey wakey seemed  to be the creators becky sloane and  joseph pelling drawing parallels to the  politics of the united states duck as a